1
00:00:34,601 --> 00:00:36,728
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
<i>Every man carries a badge.</i>

2
00:00:37,904 --> 00:00:40,202
<i>Some symbol of his allegiance.</i>

3
00:00:41,941 --> 00:00:46,901
<i>His were the scars of a boxer who'd used
his fists to climb the social ladder of the mob.</i>

4
00:00:48,348 --> 00:00:52,842
<i>A Jew who'd gained the respect of wops
through a homicidal lust.</i>

5
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,120
<i>He'd sworn an oath of violence.</i>

6
00:00:56,322 --> 00:00:57,914
<i>And his master?</i>

7
00:00:58,091 --> 00:01:00,821
<i>His own insatiable will to power.</i>

8
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:02,919
<i>He wanted to own this town.</i>

9
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:09,363
<i>His name is Mickey Cohen.</i>

10
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:19,204
<i>On my badge is the city of Los Angeles.</i>

11
00:01:19,379 --> 00:01:22,473
<i>I came back from the war
and I didn't even recognize it.</i>

12
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:27,750
<i>Brothels, vice, blood in the streets.</i>

13
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:30,151
<i>Cohen is building his empire.</i>

14
00:01:30,356 --> 00:01:32,256
"The children of the night."

15
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:33,483
<font color="#D900D9">(COYOTE HOWLING)</font>

16
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,389
"What music they make."

17
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:39,231
It's the damnedest thing, Russo.

18
00:01:39,399 --> 00:01:41,060
I come up here so many times...

19
00:01:41,968 --> 00:01:44,266
...they see me,
they know they're getting a treat.

20
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:47,929
What's the matter with you? You think they're
not gonna hear about this in Chicago?

21
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,405
Oh, I'll make sure they do.

22
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:50,838
You're certifiable, Mickey.

23
00:01:51,010 --> 00:01:54,776
You belong in a booby hatch,
eating pudding in your goddamn pajamas.

24
00:01:55,181 --> 00:01:57,240
A minute ago, you were begging.

25
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:59,282
That's when I thought you were a man.

26
00:01:59,452 --> 00:02:01,886
But you're something else.
You're rotten.

27
00:02:03,256 --> 00:02:04,814
<font color="#D900D9">(COHEN WHISTLES)</font>

28
00:02:05,692 --> 00:02:07,592
Aah!

29
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,591
What about now, Tommy?

30
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:11,588
You impressed?

31
00:02:11,764 --> 00:02:14,028
Argh! You prick bastard.

32
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,691
- Okay, boys.<font color="#808080">
RUSSO:</font> You sick son of a bitch.

33
00:02:16,903 --> 00:02:17,892
Let her rip!

34
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:20,434
Aah!

35
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:23,799
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font>
Oh, my. Heh, heh.

36
00:02:25,912 --> 00:02:28,039
Now, you go back to Chicago...

37
00:02:28,715 --> 00:02:31,047
...you tell them what you saw here tonight.

38
00:02:32,852 --> 00:02:36,652
You tell them that Los Angeles
belongs to Mickey Cohen.

39
00:02:42,795 --> 00:02:44,396
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
<i>Fighting the war had taught me...</i>

40
00:02:44,564 --> 00:02:49,968
<i>...the only thing necessary for the triumph
of evil is for good men to do nothing.</i>

41
00:02:50,303 --> 00:02:53,568
<i>People are scared.
They say leave it alone.</i>

42
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:55,230
<font color="#808080">RACINE:</font>
Excuse me, miss?

43
00:02:55,441 --> 00:02:58,035
Anyone ever tell you you look like
Lauren Bacall?

44
00:02:58,211 --> 00:02:59,200
No.

45
00:02:59,379 --> 00:03:01,711
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
<i>But Cohen isn't the only fighter.</i>

46
00:03:01,881 --> 00:03:03,849
<i>And I'm ready to step in the ring.</i>

47
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,316
Son of a bitch didn't waste any time,
did he?

48
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:09,648
Today's your lucky day.
We're holding auditions.

49
00:03:09,822 --> 00:03:11,881
- Really?
- Let's go.

50
00:03:14,594 --> 00:03:17,757
<font color="#808080">RACINE:</font> This is it.<font color="#808080">
WOMAN:</font> Ooh, wow.

51
00:03:17,931 --> 00:03:18,920
This is wonderful.

52
00:03:19,098 --> 00:03:21,658
Thank you. I can't wait to let
my folks know about this.

53
00:03:21,834 --> 00:03:23,514
<font color="#808080">RACINE:</font>
They're gonna be real proud of you.

54
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:26,036
You know, this is where
Bacall first met Bogart.

55
00:03:26,973 --> 00:03:28,270
What the hell are you doing?

56
00:03:28,474 --> 00:03:31,272
What's it look like? He's gonna
give her a bad time in there.

57
00:03:31,477 --> 00:03:34,878
O'Mara, for chrissakes, that's Cohen's
place. Nobody goes in there.

58
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,845
I don't want any part of this.

59
00:03:37,016 --> 00:03:38,415
Go get an ice cream.

60
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:44,785
<font color="#D900D9">(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)</font>

61
00:03:45,625 --> 00:03:47,115
Right this way.

62
00:03:49,095 --> 00:03:52,064
You know, we hold all our screen tests
up here, kiddo.

63
00:03:52,799 --> 00:03:54,596
Away from the crowds.

64
00:03:55,001 --> 00:03:56,059
Come on.

65
00:03:59,272 --> 00:04:02,036
- Help you with something, pal?
- Looking to meet someone.

66
00:04:02,208 --> 00:04:04,039
Yeah? What's her name?

67
00:04:05,278 --> 00:04:08,213
I don't know, I thought maybe you
could help me out with that.

68
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:13,575
- No, mister. It's okay, really.<font color="#808080">
RACINE:</font> Get in the goddamn room.

69
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:15,473
- Look at what Daddy found.<font color="#808080">
VACAREZZA:</font> Nice.

70
00:04:15,888 --> 00:04:17,253
<font color="#D900D9">(ELEVATOR DINGS)</font>

71
00:04:18,124 --> 00:04:19,751
I tell you I was partial to blonds?

72
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:23,418
Yeah, yeah, yeah. All right, big guy.
Pistola, butt-first.

73
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,261
Whoa, whoa, whoa. You're a cop?

74
00:04:26,432 --> 00:04:28,730
Christ, buddy. What are you,
soft in the head?

75
00:04:28,901 --> 00:04:30,027
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOT)</font>

76
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,935
Please! Let me go! Please! Aah!

77
00:04:50,423 --> 00:04:51,515
Aah!

78
00:04:51,691 --> 00:04:53,488
<font color="#808080">RACINE:</font> Break her, boys.<font color="#808080">
WOMAN:</font> Let me go!

79
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:57,622
No! No! Stop it, please! Don't!
Please! Please!

80
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:59,196
<font color="#D900D9">(KNOCKING ON DOOR)</font>

81
00:04:59,365 --> 00:05:01,162
- Help!<font color="#808080">
RACINE:</font> Shh. Shh.

82
00:05:01,601 --> 00:05:04,365
You make another sound and you're dead.

83
00:05:06,005 --> 00:05:07,302
<font color="#D900D9">(KNOCKING ON DOOR)</font>

84
00:05:09,108 --> 00:05:10,598
<font color="#D900D9">(WOMAN GRUNTING)</font>

85
00:05:12,612 --> 00:05:13,670
Who is it?

86
00:05:15,181 --> 00:05:16,808
Mitts in the air!

87
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,648
Come on!

88
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:20,517
I don't think so.

89
00:05:20,687 --> 00:05:24,123
- Ten bucks says this guy ain't even heeled.<font color="#808080">
MOLINARI:</font> I'll take that bet.

90
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:27,088
Why don't you come over here
and find out. Come on.

91
00:05:29,862 --> 00:05:30,886
Bang.

92
00:05:31,698 --> 00:05:33,325
<font color="#D900D9">(LAUGHING)</font>

93
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,039
Help! Somebody!

94
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,118
<font color="#808080">WOMAN:</font>
Please help me!

95
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:07,022
Welcome to Los Angeles, ma'am.

96
00:06:11,437 --> 00:06:13,166
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Patty, it was the strangest thing.

97
00:06:13,339 --> 00:06:17,435
I arrested Whalen, next thing you know,
lickety-split, he escapes.

98
00:06:17,643 --> 00:06:19,770
Oh, really? He overpowered you again?

99
00:06:20,346 --> 00:06:22,746
- No.
- He just slipped his cuffs?

100
00:06:23,349 --> 00:06:25,544
He sure did. It was the damnedest thing.

101
00:06:26,252 --> 00:06:27,241
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Keep moving.

102
00:06:29,355 --> 00:06:30,788
What happened to you this time?

103
00:06:30,957 --> 00:06:31,946
He resisted.

104
00:06:32,158 --> 00:06:33,853
Oh, yeah? What happened to them?

105
00:06:34,026 --> 00:06:35,357
They resisted.

106
00:06:36,028 --> 00:06:37,290
You're working too hard.

107
00:06:40,299 --> 00:06:41,357
Boys.

108
00:06:41,601 --> 00:06:45,093
<font color="#808080">QUINCANNON:</font>
O'Mara! Get your Irish ass in here!

109
00:06:50,209 --> 00:06:52,473
Weren't you told to stay away
from Cohen's turf?

110
00:06:52,678 --> 00:06:53,736
I was.

111
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:56,575
Hendricks told me you walked in there
without a warrant.

112
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:58,808
- These three are gonna walk.
- Says who?

113
00:07:00,486 --> 00:07:01,544
Says Judge Carter.

114
00:07:04,957 --> 00:07:07,255
Habeas corpus. Well, that's fast work.

115
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:10,487
I didn't know any better, I'd think
someone here stiffed in a call.

116
00:07:10,696 --> 00:07:13,824
Listen to me, we got rules
around here, smartass.

117
00:07:14,133 --> 00:07:16,727
Do yourself a favor: Learn them.

118
00:07:17,570 --> 00:07:20,596
Is that how you got that new Packard
out there in the parking lot?

119
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:22,400
Following the rules, boss?

120
00:07:22,575 --> 00:07:25,339
Two things you can't take back
on this job, kid:

121
00:07:25,778 --> 00:07:28,713
Bullets out of your gun
and words out of your mouth.

122
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:30,771
That it?

123
00:07:31,717 --> 00:07:32,706
Get out.

124
00:07:32,919 --> 00:07:34,978
<font color="#D900D9">(TROLLEY BELL RINGING)</font>

125
00:07:45,264 --> 00:07:46,288
Karl Lockwood.

126
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:48,429
That's Mickey's bodyguard.

127
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:51,835
I'm sure I'm not the first person
to tell you this...

128
00:07:53,105 --> 00:07:55,232
...but don't feed or tease the animals.

129
00:07:56,442 --> 00:07:58,000
Doesn't it bother you?

130
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:01,003
No.

131
00:08:04,617 --> 00:08:06,312
Not for a long time.

132
00:08:08,855 --> 00:08:10,652
Okay, stay out of trouble.

133
00:08:23,069 --> 00:08:24,161
Connie, look...

134
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:27,363
- Baby, you promised me.
- I know.

135
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:30,703
You stood right where you're standing
now and you promised me.

136
00:08:30,877 --> 00:08:32,139
I know.

137
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,347
I didn't go looking for it. Scout's honor.

138
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:47,084
John, you go looking for it every time
you leave the house.

139
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:55,560
What happened this time?

140
00:08:55,735 --> 00:08:56,929
<font color="#D900D9">(O'MARA SIGHS)</font>

141
00:08:57,169 --> 00:08:59,399
Oh, it was just some pimp.

142
00:09:01,007 --> 00:09:05,307
He was gonna put the hurt on this poor
girl who didn't know any better.

143
00:09:05,745 --> 00:09:07,542
She looked a little like you.

144
00:09:08,114 --> 00:09:10,309
I mean, not nearly as pretty, but...

145
00:09:11,017 --> 00:09:12,541
<font color="#D900D9">(O'MARA LAUGHING)</font>

146
00:09:12,952 --> 00:09:15,318
Smooth talk isn't your line, sarge.

147
00:09:17,256 --> 00:09:20,623
Look, I don't mind living like
Ma and Pa Kettle.

148
00:09:20,826 --> 00:09:22,794
I don't need a new pair of shoes every week.

149
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:24,725
I married an honest cop.

150
00:09:25,932 --> 00:09:29,891
You're kind, you don't talk too much,
you're a demon in the sack.

151
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:34,365
But I don't need a hero, sarge,
I need a husband.

152
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:38,238
So you do not have permission
to go belly-flop on a grenade.

153
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:40,641
Not when we're expecting company.
Do you read me?

154
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,609
Yeah.

155
00:09:56,862 --> 00:09:58,557
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font>
Whores don't grow on trees.

156
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:01,495
They're like mustangs.
You gotta catch them wild...

157
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:04,568
...and break them before you train them
to do tricks.

158
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:10,599
Means I need a quiet place where I can
keep the girls locked up.

159
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:13,643
Keep them hopped up on Mexican dope.

160
00:10:14,013 --> 00:10:16,243
Watch your jacket, it's filthy here.

161
00:10:16,415 --> 00:10:19,509
But this cop comes out of nowhere
like an early frost.

162
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:24,279
<font color="#D900D9">(WOMEN GROANING)</font>

163
00:10:24,824 --> 00:10:27,156
And now my whole crop of cunt
is ruined.

164
00:10:27,827 --> 00:10:30,625
Mr. Cohen, I swear to God...

165
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:35,093
You're talking to God, Mitch,
so you might as well swear to me.

166
00:10:38,404 --> 00:10:41,805
I swear, if it hadn't been for that cop,
this would have never happened.

167
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:44,408
You think I'm sore about that cop?
Hell no.

168
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,175
He's a square Joe, the guy.

169
00:10:48,514 --> 00:10:50,141
Rescues a damsel in distress.

170
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:53,444
Goddamn hero is what he is.
They should put a medal on him.

171
00:10:55,788 --> 00:10:58,723
We're gonna have to find a whole
new place. Start over again.

172
00:10:58,924 --> 00:11:00,687
It's like they say:

173
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:05,957
"All good things must one day be burnt
to the ground for the insurance money."

174
00:11:06,866 --> 00:11:08,333
<font color="#D900D9">(MEN CHUCKLING)</font>

175
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:10,196
Mr. Cohen, thank you so much.

176
00:11:10,369 --> 00:11:12,701
I swear it won't ever happen again.

177
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:14,362
I know it won't, kid.

178
00:11:15,307 --> 00:11:17,537
<font color="#808080">RACINE:</font>
Whoa. Karl, what are you doing?

179
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:18,836
<font color="#808080">MOLINARI:</font>
Let us out of here!

180
00:11:21,447 --> 00:11:23,574
<font color="#D900D9">(ALL SCREAMING)</font>

181
00:11:42,168 --> 00:11:43,226
<font color="#808080">PETE:</font>
Hey!

182
00:11:43,402 --> 00:11:45,927
Hey, Jerry. Want a shine?

183
00:11:46,105 --> 00:11:48,835
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Hey, Pete, you want a shiner? Go to bed.

184
00:11:49,008 --> 00:11:50,873
<font color="#808080">PETE:</font>
Come on, I'm a working man just like you.

185
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:53,841
How many times I gotta tell you?
When it gets dark, go home.

186
00:11:54,013 --> 00:11:57,608
I'd love to, but I gotta make just
one more buck before I can get out of here.

187
00:11:57,783 --> 00:12:00,047
- If I give you a dollar, will you go home?
- Yeah.

188
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:01,516
- Do you promise?
- I promise.

189
00:12:01,687 --> 00:12:02,779
Beat it.

190
00:12:02,988 --> 00:12:05,354
<font color="#808080">PETE:</font>
Shine? Want a shine?

191
00:12:05,858 --> 00:12:07,723
<font color="#D900D9">(PEOPLE CHATTERING)</font>

192
00:12:08,694 --> 00:12:10,389
<font color="#808080">DOORMAN:</font>
Go ahead, detective.

193
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:13,362
<font color="#D900D9">(BAND PLAYING "MR. FIVE BY FIVE")</font>

194
00:12:14,133 --> 00:12:16,363
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font> Hey, sugar.<font color="#808080">
WOMAN 1:</font> Hey, Jerry.

195
00:12:17,269 --> 00:12:21,000
<font color="#808080">WOMAN 2:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(SINGING)</font>
<i>Here comes Mr. Five By Five</i>

196
00:12:21,307 --> 00:12:22,638
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Ladies.

197
00:12:24,376 --> 00:12:27,072
<font color="#808080">WOMAN 2:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(SINGING)</font>
<i>Solid avoirdupois</i>

198
00:12:27,446 --> 00:12:30,904
<i>Mr. Five By Five</i>

199
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:35,042
<i>He's 5 feet tall and he's 5 feet wide</i>

200
00:12:35,221 --> 00:12:38,884
<i>He don't measure no more from head to toe</i>

201
00:12:39,058 --> 00:12:41,754
<i>Than he do from side to side</i>

202
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:44,395
<i>Mr. Five By Five</i>

203
00:12:44,563 --> 00:12:47,054
Jack. Fancy seeing you here.

204
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:48,598
<font color="#808080">JACK:</font>
Fancy that.

205
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:50,766
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
You look sharp.

206
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:53,268
<font color="#808080">JACK:</font> Take a pew.
- Yeah, okay.

207
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:55,172
How's it going, pal?

208
00:12:55,341 --> 00:12:58,174
You got a steak à la carte back there
with your name on it.

209
00:12:58,344 --> 00:12:59,402
You're a peach.

210
00:13:00,246 --> 00:13:01,577
Figure you must be starving.

211
00:13:01,747 --> 00:13:04,181
You haven't picked a winner in what,
six weeks?

212
00:13:04,350 --> 00:13:06,978
- Five.
- My boss can help you out with that.

213
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:11,283
You know we fix the damn races, right?
All you gotta do is ask me.

214
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,618
First, Jack, you're not allowed
to tell me that.

215
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:17,285
Second of all, you know I have
a warrant for your arrest, right?

216
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:19,590
- So, what's the charge?
- Usury.

217
00:13:20,366 --> 00:13:21,526
What the hell is usury?

218
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,759
Loansharking.
Do you want me to pull it out?

219
00:13:23,936 --> 00:13:25,870
- It's in my pocket.
- Keep it in your pants.

220
00:13:26,071 --> 00:13:29,006
- I can read it and tell you exactly what it's for.
- It's fine.

221
00:13:29,341 --> 00:13:33,141
- Jerry, can you listen to me for a second?
- Yeah, I'm listening.

222
00:13:33,445 --> 00:13:35,606
- Cohen's on the warpath.
- Warpath?

223
00:13:38,384 --> 00:13:40,852
Looks like he's on the
"give me some more" path.

224
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:46,014
<font color="#808080">JACK:</font> Just keep your eyes on the players, Jerry.
- Hard to know the players without the playbill.

225
00:13:46,358 --> 00:13:47,382
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

226
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:48,582
Okay.

227
00:13:48,761 --> 00:13:50,456
Up top you got the killer.

228
00:13:50,629 --> 00:13:52,153
Wrevock's his name.

229
00:13:52,598 --> 00:13:54,793
And down below,
the Honorable Judge Carter.

230
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:57,060
Max Solomon, Cohen's lawyer.

231
00:13:57,236 --> 00:13:59,864
And Burbank Police Chief
Elmer Jackson.

232
00:14:00,039 --> 00:14:03,406
On this side of the table,
one Eugene W. Biscailuz...

233
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,610
...the high sheriff of Los Angeles County.

234
00:14:13,819 --> 00:14:15,184
Who's the tomato?

235
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:18,680
That's Grace Faraday,
Cohen's etiquette tutor.

236
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:21,053
- Is that right?
- He's getting all sophisticated.

237
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:23,725
- Oh, must be nice.
- What's that?

238
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:26,194
I haven't been sophisticated in weeks.

239
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:27,354
<font color="#D900D9">(JACK WHISTLES)</font>

240
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,558
And it's not for lack of trying.

241
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:33,061
Roast peacock.

242
00:14:33,572 --> 00:14:37,872
Romans couldn't get enough
of this stuff. The guys had class.

243
00:14:38,444 --> 00:14:39,911
It's the other fork, darling.

244
00:14:43,849 --> 00:14:45,009
Tonight...

245
00:14:45,584 --> 00:14:49,281
...we're celebrating the birth
of a new city...

246
00:14:49,922 --> 00:14:53,756
...built right here on the ruins of
Los Angeles.

247
00:14:53,926 --> 00:14:56,258
<font color="#808080">CARTER:</font> Congratulations, Mickey.<font color="#808080">
SOLOMON:</font> Hear, hear.

248
00:14:56,929 --> 00:14:58,954
<font color="#808080">CARTER:</font> Cheers.<font color="#808080">
SOLOMON:</font> Hear, hear.

249
00:15:01,533 --> 00:15:03,865
<font color="#D900D9">(WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY)</font>

250
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:05,897
I think I'll just have a cigarette.

251
00:15:07,973 --> 00:15:09,031
Don't worry about it.

252
00:15:10,109 --> 00:15:11,406
It's done.

253
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:15,770
<font color="#808080">JACK:</font>
Don't even think about it, Jerry.

254
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:18,542
The penalty for poaching
the king's deer in this town...

255
00:15:18,717 --> 00:15:20,878
...is still a permanent vacation
in a pine box.

256
00:15:23,322 --> 00:15:25,222
Well, you gotta die of something.

257
00:15:26,392 --> 00:15:27,723
Will you excuse me?

258
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:38,596
<font color="#808080">GRACE:</font>
Thanks.

259
00:15:39,305 --> 00:15:40,431
Sure.

260
00:15:45,077 --> 00:15:46,237
I'm Jerry.

261
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:50,445
Say, Jerry, I bet you got a ducky
war story behind that lighter.

262
00:15:50,749 --> 00:15:52,614
Yeah, sure, I got stories.

263
00:15:53,585 --> 00:15:56,349
- Hey, Mac, can I get a Dirty Shirley?<font color="#808080">
BARTENDER:</font> Coming up.

264
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:59,349
I got shot down once over the Pacific.

265
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:05,158
I spent the night hanging on to the wing of the
plane, sharks bumping my legs in the dark.

266
00:16:05,331 --> 00:16:06,798
Are you weak in the knees yet?

267
00:16:07,499 --> 00:16:08,932
Sure, I am.

268
00:16:10,269 --> 00:16:13,295
Let's see. You're not quite big enough
to be a shylock.

269
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:14,598
I give up.

270
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,832
What's your racket, handsome?

271
00:16:18,243 --> 00:16:19,938
Mostly I just like to play games.

272
00:16:20,112 --> 00:16:21,670
I bet. What kind of games?

273
00:16:22,514 --> 00:16:23,947
I like to play Post Office.

274
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:26,879
Post Office? It's a kid's game.

275
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:28,943
Not the way I play it.

276
00:16:31,256 --> 00:16:33,816
But my racket is I'm a Bible salesman.

277
00:16:34,026 --> 00:16:37,655
You wanna take me away from all this
and make an honest woman out of me?

278
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:38,956
No, ma'am.

279
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:42,130
I was just hoping to take you to bed.

280
00:16:48,073 --> 00:16:51,975
<font color="#808080">MAN 1:</font> Chief! Chief, what do you think about
those girls locked up at the Croesus?

281
00:16:52,144 --> 00:16:54,104
<font color="#808080">MAN 2:</font> 
Rumor has it that was Mickey Cohen's place.

282
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:56,042
When you gonna do something
about Cohen?

283
00:16:56,215 --> 00:16:58,581
<font color="#808080">GATES:</font> Chief has no comment.<font color="#808080">
MAN 2:</font> Hey.

284
00:16:59,151 --> 00:17:01,312
Well, who's running this town, then?

285
00:17:01,487 --> 00:17:02,818
Who took it down?

286
00:17:02,988 --> 00:17:05,081
John O'Mara. Homicide.

287
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:08,217
Just one man did that?

288
00:17:08,594 --> 00:17:09,652
Yes, sir.

289
00:17:11,897 --> 00:17:13,990
<font color="#D900D9">(CHATTERING)</font>

290
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,867
<font color="#808080">GATES:</font>
Sergeant O'Mara, Daryl Gates.

291
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,562
Who the hell is Daryl Gates?

292
00:17:21,206 --> 00:17:22,434
The chief's driver.

293
00:17:23,108 --> 00:17:25,167
He'd like a word with you, sergeant.

294
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:32,214
Officer Gates, kill the fatted calf,
will you?

295
00:17:32,751 --> 00:17:35,379
I've found my prodigal son.

296
00:17:36,021 --> 00:17:37,420
Two Purple Hearts.

297
00:17:38,424 --> 00:17:40,016
Silver Star.

298
00:17:41,093 --> 00:17:42,355
Trained at Camp X?

299
00:17:43,195 --> 00:17:44,719
I never heard of Camp X, sir.

300
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,759
Of course not.

301
00:17:47,266 --> 00:17:49,826
But you are skilled in guerilla warfare.

302
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:52,927
All due respect, sir,
may I ask why I'm here?

303
00:17:53,105 --> 00:17:55,073
Would you please have a seat,
sergeant?

304
00:17:56,375 --> 00:17:59,538
I want to talk to you about the war...

305
00:18:00,379 --> 00:18:02,540
...for the soul of Los Angeles.

306
00:18:04,149 --> 00:18:08,984
You see, our forbearers fought
savage Indians and Mexican bandits...

307
00:18:09,154 --> 00:18:11,315
...to win Los Angeles.

308
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:16,223
And now, we're losing her to an
Eastern crook.

309
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:19,287
No one will testify.

310
00:18:20,866 --> 00:18:22,891
They know it's suicide.

311
00:18:23,735 --> 00:18:25,760
This isn't a crime wave.

312
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:31,240
It's enemy occupation, and you've
fought in occupied territory before.

313
00:18:32,177 --> 00:18:33,166
I have.

314
00:18:33,378 --> 00:18:35,471
I need you to do it again.

315
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:40,274
To wage guerilla war against
Mickey Cohen.

316
00:18:40,686 --> 00:18:42,586
We're finally going after him.

317
00:18:42,754 --> 00:18:43,778
I'll need men.

318
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:46,447
Recruit them. And keep it quiet.

319
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:48,456
You're off the books.

320
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:51,292
You are to make no arrests.

321
00:18:52,297 --> 00:18:54,094
- You want me to kill him?
- No.

322
00:18:54,266 --> 00:18:56,166
With Cohen dead...

323
00:18:56,335 --> 00:18:59,793
...his empire would only attract
others of his kind.

324
00:19:00,606 --> 00:19:04,133
I want you to shatter his operations...

325
00:19:04,309 --> 00:19:07,107
...destroy his establishments...

326
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:11,147
...and drive that bastard out of this city.

327
00:19:11,783 --> 00:19:13,045
Yes, sir.

328
00:19:24,129 --> 00:19:25,653
What are those?

329
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,333
I'm supposed to recruit a few guys
for this new outfit.

330
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:32,663
Oh, yeah?

331
00:19:32,938 --> 00:19:34,462
What kind of outfit?

332
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:37,838
A small squad. Five, maybe six guys.

333
00:19:40,445 --> 00:19:41,935
What kind of outfit?

334
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:47,382
We're going after Mickey Cohen.

335
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:53,491
Oh.

336
00:19:59,965 --> 00:20:01,455
<font color="#D900D9">(PLATES SHATTERING)</font>

337
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:05,397
Oh, Connie, Jesus.

338
00:20:05,837 --> 00:20:09,238
We moved out here, you said we'd found
paradise, remember?

339
00:20:10,342 --> 00:20:14,108
Wind was right, you could smell
the ocean right through that window.

340
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:19,407
That's exactly what kept me going when
I was over there, was raising a family here.

341
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:22,911
You can't ask me to just hand it
all over to Mickey Cohen.

342
00:20:23,088 --> 00:20:24,612
Mickey Cohen can have L.A., John.

343
00:20:24,790 --> 00:20:27,623
As far as I'm concerned,
he's welcome to the whole lousy town.

344
00:20:27,793 --> 00:20:28,919
He just can't have you.

345
00:20:33,365 --> 00:20:35,026
Sweetheart, look.

346
00:20:36,602 --> 00:20:38,092
The war is over.

347
00:20:40,005 --> 00:20:41,700
Stop fighting.

348
00:20:42,641 --> 00:20:44,302
Come back to me.

349
00:20:45,611 --> 00:20:47,044
I'm trying.

350
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,574
I need your help.

351
00:20:51,617 --> 00:20:55,144
<font color="#D900D9">(BLUES MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS)</font>

352
00:20:57,456 --> 00:20:58,923
<font color="#D900D9">(GRACE CHUCKLING)</font>

353
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:01,389
Hey, come here for a second,
I want to ask you something.

354
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,551
<font color="#D900D9">(GRACE KISSING)</font>

355
00:21:04,563 --> 00:21:05,962
Well, you see, the thing is...

356
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:12,630
I bet you say that to all the girls.

357
00:21:12,804 --> 00:21:13,896
I don't...

358
00:21:17,342 --> 00:21:19,435
...know what you're talking about.

359
00:21:22,914 --> 00:21:25,474
Where have you been all my miserable life...

360
00:21:27,819 --> 00:21:30,151
...Jerry the Bible salesman?

361
00:21:33,058 --> 00:21:34,286
Drinking.

362
00:21:36,795 --> 00:21:38,660
That's a noble profession.

363
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:52,837
He'll kill you if he finds out, you know.

364
00:21:55,213 --> 00:21:56,271
Who?

365
00:21:58,450 --> 00:21:59,678
Mickey.

366
00:22:04,456 --> 00:22:05,889
Mickey Mouse?

367
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:12,653
What are you doing
with that knucklehead, anyway?

368
00:22:13,231 --> 00:22:15,597
Doesn't really seem like your type.

369
00:22:19,037 --> 00:22:20,629
I'm his type.

370
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:23,835
That's what matters.

371
00:22:38,423 --> 00:22:40,721
You are something else, you know that?

372
00:22:40,892 --> 00:22:41,984
<font color="#808080">CONNIE:</font>
Yeah.

373
00:22:45,731 --> 00:22:47,699
Top of his class. Top of his class.

374
00:22:48,066 --> 00:22:51,627
This one made detective before his
30th birthday.

375
00:22:52,671 --> 00:22:55,663
If I'm Cohen, these are the cops
I'm gonna buy.

376
00:22:56,241 --> 00:22:58,072
They'll be lieutenants in a few years.

377
00:22:58,877 --> 00:23:01,846
So I should just find other bums
like me?

378
00:23:02,013 --> 00:23:06,040
I'm just saying that you shouldn't be
looking at choir boys for this.

379
00:23:08,353 --> 00:23:10,433
<font color="#D900D9">(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING
AND MEN CHEERING AND WHISTLING)</font>

380
00:23:15,961 --> 00:23:17,690
I'm putting a squad together.

381
00:23:17,863 --> 00:23:21,299
- I need an Indian guide who knows the territory.
- Oh.

382
00:23:21,466 --> 00:23:25,960
I wish I could help. I'm just in the middle
of a very important case, so I can't.

383
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:29,173
Who's the lucky winner this time?

384
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:33,908
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Mm.

385
00:23:34,179 --> 00:23:35,942
<font color="#D900D9">(LAUGHS)</font>

386
00:23:36,114 --> 00:23:37,138
Well, good luck.

387
00:23:37,315 --> 00:23:38,475
That's all you got?

388
00:23:38,683 --> 00:23:41,151
Sarge, the whole town's underwater...

389
00:23:41,319 --> 00:23:45,619
...and you're grabbing a bucket when you
should grab a bathing suit, you know?

390
00:23:45,791 --> 00:23:48,089
Come on, Jerry,
what the hell happened to you?

391
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:49,894
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Hey...

392
00:23:50,295 --> 00:23:52,263
...same thing that happened to you, pal.

393
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:56,260
But the war's over
and we don't have to fight anymore.

394
00:23:57,135 --> 00:23:59,501
You're not gonna change anything
around here, sarge.

395
00:23:59,704 --> 00:24:02,969
You're just gonna wake up one morning
on the wrong side of the grass.

396
00:24:03,141 --> 00:24:04,267
For what?

397
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:08,743
If you can't answer that question,
take off the badge.

398
00:24:13,585 --> 00:24:14,813
Drink up.

399
00:24:18,223 --> 00:24:20,521
Okay, but only because it sounded
like an order.

400
00:24:20,959 --> 00:24:24,793
<font color="#808080">CONNIE:</font> <i>How about this guy? They call him
The Sheriff of Central Avenue.</i>

401
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,362
<i>Coleman Harris.</i>

402
00:24:26,998 --> 00:24:28,989
Excessive force and insubordination.

403
00:24:29,167 --> 00:24:31,533
Sounds like a man
after your own dear heart.

404
00:24:31,736 --> 00:24:33,727
<font color="#D900D9">(UPBEAT SWING MUSIC PLAYING)</font>

405
00:24:41,379 --> 00:24:42,471
Aah!

406
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:43,671
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
It's okay, Del.

407
00:24:44,349 --> 00:24:45,816
- Now, don't wiggle it.
- Unh!

408
00:24:45,984 --> 00:24:47,815
Be best you pull it straight out.

409
00:24:49,754 --> 00:24:53,053
Lieutenant. Sergeant John O'Mara.

410
00:24:53,625 --> 00:24:55,183
Can I buy you a drink?

411
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:58,026
Well, seeing as though I'm still on duty...

412
00:24:58,196 --> 00:24:59,663
...you better buy me two.

413
00:25:05,203 --> 00:25:09,003
Damn heroin, eating Central Avenue
down to the bone.

414
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:13,637
I lost my niece to it a year ago.

415
00:25:14,579 --> 00:25:18,015
I'm the only law that there is down here.

416
00:25:18,383 --> 00:25:20,908
What would you say if I took you upriver?

417
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:23,150
All the way to the headwaters.

418
00:25:23,321 --> 00:25:24,413
No more pushers.

419
00:25:24,890 --> 00:25:26,585
Plug it up right at the source.

420
00:25:30,428 --> 00:25:32,658
- Sarge.
- What is that?

421
00:25:32,998 --> 00:25:34,192
Look.

422
00:25:34,833 --> 00:25:35,822
What?

423
00:25:36,001 --> 00:25:37,764
- Oh, no.
- Why not?

424
00:25:37,936 --> 00:25:41,736
No, you can't just pull some guy
out of a magazine like he's a decoder ring.

425
00:25:41,907 --> 00:25:42,999
You can't do that.

426
00:25:43,174 --> 00:25:48,373
Sarge, Max Kennard has shot more crooks
than any L.A. cop in the last hundred years.

427
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:52,608
Sooner or later, there's gonna be gunplay,
and I want Kennard with you when it happens.

428
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:57,878
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
Max Kennard.

429
00:25:58,723 --> 00:25:59,712
Mind if I join you?

430
00:26:00,926 --> 00:26:01,915
All right.

431
00:26:05,096 --> 00:26:06,256
Navidad Ramirez.

432
00:26:07,532 --> 00:26:09,022
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
"Christmas" Ramirez?

433
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:11,695
It's all right if you're
a burlesque dancer...

434
00:26:11,870 --> 00:26:14,771
...but I keep on telling him
it's no kind of name for a lawman.

435
00:26:14,940 --> 00:26:16,635
Mind if I talk with you for a minute?

436
00:26:18,143 --> 00:26:20,737
Go on, Navidad. Get some air.

437
00:26:25,717 --> 00:26:28,117
That kid's not gonna last long
riding with you.

438
00:26:28,286 --> 00:26:31,119
Hell, nobody'll work with him
on account of his heritage.

439
00:26:32,924 --> 00:26:34,619
I'm going after Mickey Cohen.

440
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,256
And I need a gun hand.

441
00:26:43,101 --> 00:26:44,625
Wouldn't you know it?

442
00:26:45,503 --> 00:26:47,630
I just happen to have one.

443
00:26:48,239 --> 00:26:51,640
- There it is. Good as new.
- Thanks, Dad.

444
00:26:51,810 --> 00:26:53,402
Yeah, don't crash.

445
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,372
Conwell Keeler?

446
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:58,810
Can I help you with something, fella?

447
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:03,448
You need someone with brains
to balance the brawn.

448
00:27:03,755 --> 00:27:05,518
He was Army Intelligence.

449
00:27:05,690 --> 00:27:08,488
Got demoted for not understanding
the need for a warrant.

450
00:27:08,660 --> 00:27:12,152
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font> Rocketdyne's test firing their new
missile up in Santa Susana.

451
00:27:12,330 --> 00:27:14,423
It's supposed to be faster than the V-2.

452
00:27:14,599 --> 00:27:16,260
- Thank you, ma'am.
- Thank you, baby.

453
00:27:16,434 --> 00:27:19,335
You don't know what the V-2 is,
that's okay. This one's faster.

454
00:27:20,505 --> 00:27:22,973
I heard you were the best wire man
in the department.

455
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:24,472
Oh, yeah? Thank you.

456
00:27:24,909 --> 00:27:28,401
Look, these other guys I've been asking,
none of them have families.

457
00:27:29,447 --> 00:27:30,971
So you wanna think this over?

458
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:32,980
<font color="#808080">BOY:</font> Dad! It's the rocket!
- Oh.

459
00:27:33,218 --> 00:27:35,015
<font color="#808080">BOY:</font>
Come on, hurry!

460
00:27:36,154 --> 00:27:38,850
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
Wow. Isn't she a beaut?

461
00:27:40,558 --> 00:27:41,616
<font color="#808080">BOY:</font>
Look, Dad.

462
00:27:41,993 --> 00:27:44,325
Yeah. It's pretty great, right?

463
00:27:45,697 --> 00:27:47,631
You know, this...

464
00:27:48,199 --> 00:27:49,632
...a brighter future...

465
00:27:49,801 --> 00:27:51,701
...this is what we fought for, isn't it?

466
