Floor it, Navidad!

691
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:05,788
That didn't work.

692
00:42:07,324 --> 00:42:08,848
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOT)</font>

693
00:42:10,027 --> 00:42:11,358
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOT)</font>

694
00:42:12,229 --> 00:42:13,719
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOTS)</font>

695
00:42:18,102 --> 00:42:19,660
Who's there?

696
00:42:21,238 --> 00:42:23,035
Bwana's a Swahili word.

697
00:42:23,207 --> 00:42:26,438
- Means "sir." Got it?
- Unh!

698
00:42:26,944 --> 00:42:28,036
Yes, sir.

699
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,905
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Come on, let's go, let's go.

700
00:42:38,255 --> 00:42:40,120
Now, who the fuck is this guy?

701
00:42:40,624 --> 00:42:42,057
Jerry Wooters.

702
00:42:42,226 --> 00:42:43,750
He's one of us.

703
00:42:48,032 --> 00:42:50,762
I know it doesn't look like much now.

704
00:42:51,769 --> 00:42:54,465
But this is gonna be my crown jewel.

705
00:42:54,638 --> 00:42:56,606
Welcome to El Dorado Trust.

706
00:42:57,107 --> 00:43:01,305
We're standing in the middle
of a money-making machine.

707
00:43:01,478 --> 00:43:02,638
Makes me giddy.

708
00:43:03,047 --> 00:43:05,242
We got all the whores and dope sewn up.

709
00:43:05,416 --> 00:43:07,816
But pari-mutuel wagering, bang.

710
00:43:07,985 --> 00:43:10,112
Off-track betting, ba-bang.

711
00:43:10,287 --> 00:43:12,221
That's where the real money is.

712
00:43:12,389 --> 00:43:14,550
Have this place open in a few weeks.

713
00:43:14,725 --> 00:43:18,821
After that, all the wire traffic west
of Chicago comes right through here.

714
00:43:18,996 --> 00:43:20,054
Millions.

715
00:43:20,230 --> 00:43:23,097
I couldn't make it any faster if I was
printing it myself.

716
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:24,890
What about the Syndicate?

717
00:43:25,069 --> 00:43:27,833
That's the past. This is the future.

718
00:43:28,005 --> 00:43:31,406
I'll buy them off with money we pull
out of this place alone.

719
00:43:31,675 --> 00:43:33,836
Buy every politician from here to Frisco.

720
00:43:34,011 --> 00:43:37,674
Within a month, we'll have the whole
West Coast tied up in a nice ribbon.

721
00:43:50,427 --> 00:43:51,689
<font color="#D900D9">(SILENCED GUNSHOT)</font>

722
00:43:54,665 --> 00:43:55,757
Come on.

723
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:00,457
<font color="#D900D9">(SILENCED GUNSHOTS
AND MAN GRUNTS)</font>

724
00:44:10,214 --> 00:44:12,546
<font color="#D900D9">(SILENCED GUNSHOTS
AND WOMAN SCREAMS)</font>

725
00:44:15,953 --> 00:44:17,853
<font color="#D900D9">(GROANING)</font>

726
00:44:26,030 --> 00:44:27,827
All right? Your turn.

727
00:44:35,572 --> 00:44:37,301
You gonna break leather, Hopalong?

728
00:44:37,474 --> 00:44:39,305
Or you just gonna watch us?

729
00:44:48,152 --> 00:44:51,986
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOTS)</font>

730
00:44:53,257 --> 00:44:54,554
<font color="#808080">RAMIREZ:</font>
You were saying?

731
00:44:54,858 --> 00:44:56,826
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
Get on up here, Navidad.

732
00:44:58,028 --> 00:44:59,461
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Sheesh.

733
00:45:00,230 --> 00:45:01,595
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
You loaded?

734
00:45:04,968 --> 00:45:06,868
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOTS)</font>

735
00:45:09,907 --> 00:45:12,171
Don't shoot where it is, son.

736
00:45:12,743 --> 00:45:14,608
Shoot where it's gonna be.

737
00:45:17,414 --> 00:45:18,779
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOT AND CAN RATTLES)</font>

738
00:45:19,616 --> 00:45:21,049
<font color="#D900D9">(KENNARD GROANS)</font>

739
00:45:23,253 --> 00:45:24,686
<font color="#D900D9">(HORN HONKING)</font>

740
00:45:30,928 --> 00:45:32,395
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
They got Dragna.

741
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:34,793
They killed everybody in the house.

742
00:45:35,132 --> 00:45:38,226
His wife. Killed the maid, for chrissake.

743
00:45:38,769 --> 00:45:42,068
Cohen must have thought what we did
to his casino was Dragna's guys.

744
00:45:42,239 --> 00:45:43,729
This was payback.

745
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:45,708
It's war. People die.

746
00:45:47,010 --> 00:45:50,036
I'm sorry, I can't believe you would
say something like that.

747
00:45:50,514 --> 00:45:52,812
Sarge, I don't want any more
civilian casualties.

748
00:45:53,016 --> 00:45:54,142
Then talk to Cohen.

749
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:56,049
I'd rather listen to him.

750
00:45:56,220 --> 00:45:59,383
All we do is plant a bug and we can
hear everything he says.

751
00:46:01,458 --> 00:46:03,016
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
One of the clubs?

752
00:46:03,393 --> 00:46:04,655
No, his house.

753
00:46:14,738 --> 00:46:17,639
<font color="#D900D9">(WHISPERING)</font> It takes him three minutes
to get around the house. Go.

754
00:46:43,834 --> 00:46:46,359
<font color="#808080">MAN 1:</font> 
Hey, guys, do you want in on this?

755
00:46:46,570 --> 00:46:49,562
<font color="#808080">MAN 2:</font> You owe me 10 bucks from last night.<font color="#808080">
MAN 3:</font> You always say that.

756
00:46:50,307 --> 00:46:51,547
<font color="#808080">MAN 1:</font> 
We're here to play cards.

757
00:46:51,675 --> 00:46:54,075
- So five-card draw?<font color="#808080">
MAN 3:</font> Sounds good.

758
00:47:08,192 --> 00:47:11,184
<font color="#D900D9">(WHISPERING)</font> - What are you doing?
- Just looking at a picture.

759
00:47:18,135 --> 00:47:21,195
Cohen's home. Get out now. Get out.

760
00:47:31,381 --> 00:47:32,541
Dessert, Mr. Cohen?

761
00:47:32,716 --> 00:47:34,843
Oh, hot fudge sundae.

762
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:39,084
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font>
Let's taste that, yeah. Mm.

763
00:47:39,256 --> 00:47:40,746
You're the best.

764
00:47:41,058 --> 00:47:43,526
- I'm just gonna powder my nose.<font color="#808080">
COHEN:</font> Whatever.

765
00:47:48,498 --> 00:47:49,624
Shh.

766
00:48:08,085 --> 00:48:10,212
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Hey, Mickey. Anybody home?

767
00:48:12,456 --> 00:48:14,515
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(OVER RADIO)</font>
<i>Karl, I wanna take a look at that property.</i>

768
00:48:14,691 --> 00:48:17,854
<i>- That bakery down near Boyle Heights.</i><font color="#808080">
KARL:</font> <i>You got it, Mickey.</i>

769
00:48:18,729 --> 00:48:20,697
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font> Hi.<font color="#808080">
O'MARA:</font> You heard anything?

770
00:48:20,864 --> 00:48:23,230
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font> Apparently, Johnny Stomp's
balling Lana Turner.

771
00:48:23,400 --> 00:48:25,527
Sinatra sounds pretty sore about it.

772
00:48:25,702 --> 00:48:30,401
Judge Carter is a world-class whoremonger
and Mickey takes good care of him.

773
00:48:30,574 --> 00:48:31,563
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Figures.

774
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:34,370
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font> Those are the locations of some of the
books around town.

775
00:48:34,544 --> 00:48:37,672
There must be a ton of them.
He's building something.

776
00:48:37,881 --> 00:48:39,746
I don't know what it is yet.

777
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:41,817
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Okay, well, we gotta find it.

778
00:48:42,119 --> 00:48:44,053
No. Don't touch that.

779
00:48:44,221 --> 00:48:45,483
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Get some grub.

780
00:48:47,791 --> 00:48:49,884
You got something to tell me, Romeo?

781
00:48:52,129 --> 00:48:53,460
It's nothing.

782
00:48:55,098 --> 00:48:56,395
It didn't look like nothing.

783
00:48:56,566 --> 00:48:57,726
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
What the hell is this?

784
00:48:57,901 --> 00:49:00,893
Hey, guys, guys. I just heard
something about a heroin shipment. Shh.

785
00:49:01,071 --> 00:49:03,505
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font> Let me hear. Let me hear.<font color="#808080">
KEELER:</font> Here.

786
00:49:03,740 --> 00:49:05,401
<font color="#D900D9">(INDISTINCT DIALOGUE ON HEADSET)</font>

787
00:49:05,575 --> 00:49:08,635
- I can't hear it, Con. Turn it up.
- Well, it's up all the way.

788
00:49:08,812 --> 00:49:11,474
- I can't hear anything.
- I think they're leaving the room.

789
00:49:11,648 --> 00:49:14,082
- Oh, come on.
- Yeah, they left the room.

790
00:49:14,251 --> 00:49:15,343
Shit.

791
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:20,916
- Where. We need to know where.<font color="#808080">
KEELER:</font> I don't know. I'll keep listening.

792
00:49:21,091 --> 00:49:22,811
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font> I know a guy who can tell us.
- Who?

793
00:49:23,527 --> 00:49:25,290
Old friend from the neighborhood.

794
00:49:25,629 --> 00:49:26,618
Unh!

795
00:49:26,797 --> 00:49:29,425
Cohen's got some medicine coming.
Where's he bringing it in?

796
00:49:29,599 --> 00:49:31,624
I don't know! Aah!

797
00:49:31,802 --> 00:49:33,599
- Don't lie to me, boy.
<font color="#808080">DEL-RED:</font> Wait, wait!

798
00:49:33,770 --> 00:49:35,032
Harris, they'll kill me.

799
00:49:35,238 --> 00:49:38,469
Not if you leave town, they won't.
Now, start talking.

800
00:49:40,277 --> 00:49:42,472
Burbank Airport, Friday night.

801
00:49:42,646 --> 00:49:44,045
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font> You sure?
- Yes!

802
00:49:44,247 --> 00:49:47,478
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
All right. Get your ass out of here. Damn.

803
00:49:48,485 --> 00:49:50,885
I can't believe we going back to Burbank.

804
00:49:55,892 --> 00:49:57,951
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
That stuff is Mickey's poison.

805
00:49:58,128 --> 00:50:00,358
We shut it down, we take away
his best weapon.

806
00:50:00,530 --> 00:50:02,964
<font color="#D900D9">(MEN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)</font>

807
00:50:03,467 --> 00:50:04,798
<font color="#808080">COP:</font>
Let me get that for you, sir.

808
00:50:11,174 --> 00:50:12,539
<font color="#808080">GRIMES:</font>
We good?

809
00:50:15,645 --> 00:50:17,078
All right, let's go.

810
00:50:18,415 --> 00:50:19,712
Come on.

811
00:50:26,056 --> 00:50:28,581
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font> Let's just wait until they get over
the river into L.A.

812
00:50:28,859 --> 00:50:31,692
I think we've worn out our welcome
with the Burbank P.D.

813
00:50:37,934 --> 00:50:39,492
Forget it, let's take them now.

814
00:50:43,507 --> 00:50:45,839
Looks like we picked up
a couple of ticks.

815
00:50:46,410 --> 00:50:47,934
Let's burn them off the road.

816
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:53,311
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
Shit!

817
00:50:54,384 --> 00:50:55,783
Oh, my God!

818
00:50:55,952 --> 00:50:57,214
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Everybody get down!

819
00:50:58,889 --> 00:51:00,857
Hold on to your hats, boys!

820
00:51:01,958 --> 00:51:03,425
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
Ah! Jesus Christ!

821
00:51:11,268 --> 00:51:12,599
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
Take them out!

822
00:51:16,440 --> 00:51:18,101
Ah!

823
00:51:24,614 --> 00:51:26,215
<font color="#808080">RAMIREZ:</font>
You're giving them a clear shot!

824
00:51:26,550 --> 00:51:29,383
- All right, that's it!
- Where the hell is he going?

825
00:51:30,153 --> 00:51:31,234
<font color="#808080">RAMIREZ:</font>
Get out of the way!

826
00:51:31,388 --> 00:51:32,616
What the hell's he doing?

827
00:51:32,889 --> 00:51:34,151
<font color="#808080">RAMIREZ:</font>
Move over!

828
00:51:43,400 --> 00:51:44,680
<font color="#808080">GRIMES:</font>
Where the hell did he go?

829
00:51:45,068 --> 00:51:46,467
- You see him?
- No, sir!

830
00:51:46,636 --> 00:51:47,898
<font color="#808080">GRIMES:</font>
Damn it, you see him?

831
00:51:50,073 --> 00:51:51,165
Jesus!

832
00:51:52,275 --> 00:51:53,469
Oh, shit!

833
00:52:09,526 --> 00:52:10,686
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
What the hell is that?

834
00:52:11,828 --> 00:52:12,988
Shit!

835
00:52:14,264 --> 00:52:15,697
Jesus Christ!

836
00:52:16,199 --> 00:52:18,167
John, back off! Back off!

837
00:52:20,537 --> 00:52:21,629
Grenade! Shit!

838
00:52:23,773 --> 00:52:24,797
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Grab it!

839
00:52:33,950 --> 00:52:34,974
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Hit him harder!

840
00:52:38,321 --> 00:52:39,413
All right, hang on.

841
00:52:40,690 --> 00:52:42,681
Unh! Son of a bitch. No!

842
00:52:48,465 --> 00:52:49,727
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
Okay.

843
00:52:50,834 --> 00:52:52,358
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
Closer, Navidad!

844
00:52:52,802 --> 00:52:54,167
Shit.

845
00:53:09,153 --> 00:53:10,745
<font color="#D900D9">(GRUNTING)</font>

846
00:53:11,822 --> 00:53:13,380
<font color="#808080">KENNARD:</font>
Let's go, hoss.

847
00:53:14,692 --> 00:53:16,557
- Where do you want them?<font color="#808080">
O'MARA:</font> Right here.

848
00:53:19,196 --> 00:53:20,493
Who the hell are you?

849
00:53:20,664 --> 00:53:24,156
You don't know what you done, pal.
You think he's gonna laugh this off?

850
00:53:24,335 --> 00:53:25,734
He will hunt you down.

851
00:53:25,903 --> 00:53:29,771
- That's not your problem anymore. You hear me?
- Ah!

852
00:53:29,974 --> 00:53:32,772
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.
- You have their wallets? What are their names?

853
00:53:32,977 --> 00:53:35,104
Edgar Beaumont and Jeffrey Clark.

854
00:53:35,279 --> 00:53:36,507
We know who you are.

855
00:53:36,680 --> 00:53:39,615
You used to run dope for Mickey Cohen.
You're retired.

856
00:53:40,417 --> 00:53:42,510
<font color="#D900D9">(BEAUMONT SCREAMS)</font>

857
00:53:48,692 --> 00:53:50,421
<font color="#D900D9">(GRUNTING)</font>

858
00:53:52,363 --> 00:53:53,887
Let's get out of here.

859
00:54:06,110 --> 00:54:09,307
You really wanna win this thing,
or you wanna die trying?

860
00:54:09,513 --> 00:54:14,212
Don't get me wrong, I love shooting gangsters
in the legs just as much as the next guy.

861
00:54:14,385 --> 00:54:16,444
But we're gonna have to be smarter
next time.

862
00:54:17,021 --> 00:54:20,889
Playing hot potato with a grenade
isn't much of a strategy.

863
00:54:23,160 --> 00:54:25,060
We got really lucky.

864
00:54:25,729 --> 00:54:29,597
If we keep going head-on at him like this,
we're not gonna make it more than a week.

865
00:54:30,334 --> 00:54:31,767
It worked, Jerry.

866
00:54:32,303 --> 00:54:33,736
Get in the car.

867
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:46,848
Mr. Cohen, sir. I.... The, uh....

868
00:54:47,051 --> 00:54:50,179
Someone hit the shipment.

869
00:54:50,354 --> 00:54:51,821
I'm sorry.

870
00:54:55,092 --> 00:54:56,354
Who hit the shipment?

871
00:54:56,827 --> 00:54:59,591
Guineas from back East.
Maybe Russo's people.

872
00:54:59,763 --> 00:55:02,061
- I don't know.<font color="#808080">
COHEN:</font> Hm.

873
00:55:02,833 --> 00:55:04,994
Maybe Russo's people.

874
00:55:07,304 --> 00:55:08,362
Well....

875
00:55:11,108 --> 00:55:12,575
These things happen.

876
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:16,973
- Tsk.<font color="#808080">
GRIMES:</font> Thank you, Mr. Cohen.

877
00:55:18,882 --> 00:55:19,940
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font>
Karl.

878
00:55:20,684 --> 00:55:22,345
You know the drill.

879
00:55:23,854 --> 00:55:25,549
<font color="#808080">GRIMES:</font>
No! No! Karl, no!

880
00:55:25,723 --> 00:55:27,190
Hey, Karl! No!

881
00:55:27,891 --> 00:55:29,882
- I'm begging you!<font color="#808080">
KARL:</font> You stupid bastard.

882
00:55:30,728 --> 00:55:34,220
<font color="#808080">GRIMES:</font>
This ain't right! This ain't right! Aah!

883
00:55:36,100 --> 00:55:38,781
<font color="#D900D9">(KITTY DAISY & LEWIS' "A LITTLE BIRD
TOLD ME" PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS)</font>

884
00:55:38,902 --> 00:55:42,531
<i>Fallin' for no one but you</i>

885
00:55:43,741 --> 00:55:46,175
<i>There's no use denying</i>

886
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:47,970
<i>I might as well confess</i>

887
00:55:48,145 --> 00:55:49,669
<font color="#808080">CONNIE:</font> Come in.
- Mrs. O'Mara?

888
00:55:50,314 --> 00:55:51,713
Please, Connie.

889
00:55:51,882 --> 00:55:54,316
Jerry Wooters. Nice to meet you.

890
00:55:54,485 --> 00:55:56,851
Nice to meet you too. What'd you bring?

891
00:55:57,488 --> 00:55:58,716
Bear claws.

892
00:56:01,759 --> 00:56:03,158
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Uh....

893
00:56:04,027 --> 00:56:05,358
Congratulations. I didn't....

894
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:07,929
Thank you. John didn't tell you?

895
00:56:08,632 --> 00:56:09,758
No, he didn't.

896
00:56:09,933 --> 00:56:11,924
- Where is that guy?
- Out back.

897
00:56:12,136 --> 00:56:13,398
Okay.

898
00:56:14,037 --> 00:56:18,167
<i>This little bird told me when we marry</i>

899
00:56:18,342 --> 00:56:19,775
Jerry?

900
00:56:19,943 --> 00:56:20,932
Yeah?

901
00:56:21,145 --> 00:56:26,242
I know. What kind of a guy would take on
a job like this with his wife in my condition?

902
00:56:26,583 --> 00:56:27,743
That kind of guy.

903
00:56:28,886 --> 00:56:33,346
My husband's the bravest man I know
but he is not much for abstract thinking.

904
00:56:33,524 --> 00:56:35,890
Honor and duty are as real as I am.

905
00:56:36,460 --> 00:56:39,452
So if it comes down to a choice
between his life and his duty...

906
00:56:39,663 --> 00:56:41,927
You want me to push him
in the right direction?

907
00:56:42,399 --> 00:56:44,279
- Can I shove him in the right direction?
- Heh.

908
00:56:44,401 --> 00:56:46,528
That's why I picked you. You seem sensible.

909
00:56:46,703 --> 00:56:48,261
Well, that's a nice way to put it.

910
00:56:48,439 --> 00:56:50,805
I handpicked all of you guys,
except the Mexican kid.

911
00:56:50,974 --> 00:56:54,774
- I don't know where you found him.
- I don't know where he came from either.

912
00:56:56,713 --> 00:56:58,044
Take that out?

913
00:56:58,282 --> 00:56:59,977
John's a lucky guy, Connie.

914
00:57:04,121 --> 00:57:05,202
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Look, you know what?

915
00:57:05,322 --> 00:57:07,187
You should get your wife a Cadillac.

916
00:57:07,591 --> 00:57:09,388
How's your love life these days?

917
00:57:09,560 --> 00:57:11,040
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Your wife deserves a Cadillac.

918
00:57:11,195 --> 00:57:15,097
You're driving a Studebaker, you should
buy yourself a Cadillac. It's a nice car.

919
00:57:15,265 --> 00:57:17,096
You don't get cars like that too often.

920
00:57:17,501 --> 00:57:20,902
You know, Jerry, one of these nights
she's just gonna get bored.

921
00:57:21,238 --> 00:57:22,500
Scared.

922
00:57:23,340 --> 00:57:27,208
Or he'll give her a rock and she'll
just roll on us in a fit of gratitude.

923
00:57:28,245 --> 00:57:31,442
Or he'll just find out she's got
a new swain and that's not good.

924
00:57:34,751 --> 00:57:39,620
With all due respect, sarge, you don't
know a goddamn thing about her.

925
00:57:40,257 --> 00:57:41,349
Gentlemen.

926
00:57:42,626 --> 00:57:46,494
I would congratulate you
on a job well done.

927
00:57:47,798 --> 00:57:50,130
But then I was never here.

928
00:57:50,968 --> 00:57:53,766
Cohen has already organized a dragnet.

929
00:57:53,937 --> 00:57:56,030
He has his people inside the department...

930
00:57:56,240 --> 00:57:59,141
...hunting for the gang
that hit his drug shipment.

931
00:57:59,510 --> 00:58:03,002
It's only a matter of time until
he realizes you're cops.

932
00:58:03,780 --> 00:58:07,181
We need to step up our timetable here,
sergeant.

933
00:58:07,484 --> 00:58:10,044
We need to offer Cohen no quarter.

934
00:58:10,254 --> 00:58:11,846
I'm not a quarter kind of guy, sir.

935
00:58:12,322 --> 00:58:13,346
Neither am I.

936
00:58:37,314 --> 00:58:38,838
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font>
Unh!

937
00:58:52,029 --> 00:58:53,018
Get out!

938
00:59:04,908 --> 00:59:06,034
<font color="#D900D9">(INDISTINCT DIALOGUE)</font>

939
00:59:28,532 --> 00:59:29,760
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font>
Over there.

940
00:59:30,901 --> 00:59:33,961
Telephones, wires. Hey, hey.

941
00:59:34,137 --> 00:59:36,367
You are dead, pal. You are all dea...

942
00:59:39,042 --> 00:59:40,373
Yeah, we get that a lot.

943
01:00:01,732 --> 01:00:03,962
Find these bastards.

944
01:00:05,235 --> 01:00:06,759
Kill them all.

945
01:00:07,604 --> 01:00:09,265
Kill their families.

946
01:00:09,439 --> 01:00:10,565
Their kids.

947
01:00:10,741 --> 01:00:12,606
<i>Their dogs. Their cats.</i>

948
01:00:12,776 --> 01:00:15,142
<i>They're on the scent of El Dorado Trust.</i>

949
01:00:15,312 --> 01:00:19,180
<i>We cannot let that happen.
Do you understand me?</i>

950
01:00:20,751 --> 01:00:25,620
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
El Dorado Trust.

951
01:00:26,323 --> 01:00:27,813
It's an A-bomb.

952
01:00:28,458 --> 01:00:30,517
It's Mickey Cohen's pride and joy.

953
01:00:31,328 --> 01:00:33,660
The whole reason he killed
Tommy Russo...

954
01:00:33,830 --> 01:00:36,162
...was to take over his
Continental Wire service...

955
01:00:36,466 --> 01:00:40,630
...which means Cohen's got the only wire
between here and Chicago.

956
01:00:41,405 --> 01:00:45,808
He's building the central book
for the entire western United States.

957
01:00:45,976 --> 01:00:47,841
Wait, what's the central book?

958
01:00:48,011 --> 01:00:51,469
All gambling money on the West Coast
will go through a central book...

959
01:00:51,648 --> 01:00:53,878
...and Mickey Cohen
will touch every penny.

960
01:00:54,051 --> 01:00:58,044
If he gets that thing up and running,
inside a week it won't matter what we do.

961
01:00:58,455 --> 01:01:00,787
It'll be growing faster than we can
tear it down.

962
01:01:01,324 --> 01:01:02,985
He'll own the whole goddamn state.

963
01:01:03,360 --> 01:01:04,349
Where is it?

964
01:01:05,529 --> 01:01:06,655
I don't know.

965
01:01:07,297 --> 01:01:09,026
They haven't said a thing.

966
01:01:09,366 --> 01:01:10,856
Well, we gotta find it.

967
01:01:11,034 --> 01:01:12,661
Yes, we do.

968
01:01:14,004 --> 01:01:15,631
We don't have a lot of time, Jerry.

969
01:01:27,484 --> 01:01:28,849
I'm not gonna get her killed.

970
01:01:30,020 --> 01:01:31,317
You gotta ask her.

971
01:01:31,688 --> 01:01:32,985
Or I will.

972
01:01:35,692 --> 01:01:37,990
You know, I ain't gotta
prove myself to you.

973
01:01:38,161 --> 01:01:40,391
You asked me to be here and I'm here.

974
01:01:41,064 --> 01:01:43,589
I'm risking my life,
like every single guy in there.

975
01:01:43,767 --> 01:01:44,893
But there's a line.

976
01:01:45,569 --> 01:01:46,900
You go and talk to my girl...

977
01:01:47,070 --> 01:01:50,437
...you put her in danger, you're gonna
cross that line with me, pal.

978
01:01:50,607 --> 01:01:52,973
I'm not questioning your loyalty, Jerry.

979
01:01:53,543 --> 01:01:54,874
Don't go near her.

980
01:01:55,579 --> 01:01:57,547
Just do what needs to be done.

981
01:02:13,897 --> 01:02:15,387
You're going somewhere?

982
01:02:16,933 --> 01:02:18,230
I gotta go.

983
01:02:25,275 --> 01:02:26,799
You gotta do that in front of me?

984
01:02:28,145 --> 01:02:30,773
You gotta make yourself pretty for him
in front of me?

985
01:02:32,048 --> 01:02:34,915
- What's the matter?
- You got a lot of nerve.

986
01:02:36,787 --> 01:02:38,152
What are we doing?

987
01:02:38,588 --> 01:02:40,556
I can't figure out your angle.

988
01:02:41,792 --> 01:02:42,884
What's your angle?

989
01:02:43,059 --> 01:02:45,084
What were you doing in his house, Jerry?

990
01:02:45,262 --> 01:02:46,923
You don't wanna know that.

991
01:02:49,633 --> 01:02:51,396
Why didn't you tell me you're a cop?

992
01:02:52,536 --> 01:02:53,798
I'm looking out for you.

993
01:02:53,970 --> 01:02:57,303
- Trust me.
- No. I don't trust you.

994
01:03:01,077 --> 01:03:03,102
He's gonna plant us both.

995
01:03:07,651 --> 01:03:10,677
- That stirs you a little, doesn't it?
- Oh, yeah, that stirs me up.

996
01:03:10,854 --> 01:03:14,187
- It does, Jerry, admit it.
- It stirs me right up.

997
01:03:14,791 --> 01:03:16,952
Maybe that's why you're with him.

998
01:03:17,327 --> 01:03:19,795
- You think that's why I'm with him?
- I don't know.

999
01:03:21,932 --> 01:03:24,457
I came out here to be a star, Jerry.

1000
01:03:25,635 --> 01:03:27,660
I figured I couldn't lose.

1001
01:03:31,308 --> 01:03:33,708
I figured wrong, didn't l?

1002
01:03:38,381 --> 01:03:40,576
I'm open to suggestions.

1003
01:03:41,451 --> 01:03:42,782
Don't go.

1004
01:03:43,787 --> 01:03:45,118
Don't let me.

1005
01:04:02,973 --> 01:04:06,067
<font color="#808080">HERBERT:</font>
One-two. Ho-ho. Whoa.

1006
01:04:06,243 --> 01:04:08,108
This the one where you break his jaw?

1007
01:04:10,614 --> 01:04:11,979
Hey, Claude Rains.

1008
01:04:14,718 --> 01:04:16,811
Come here,
I wanna show you something.

1009
01:04:16,987 --> 01:04:18,682
<font color="#808080">HERBERT:</font>
Hurt him. Yeah.

1010
01:04:23,727 --> 01:04:27,185
- This putz was trying to steal my title.<font color="#808080">
GRACE:</font> Heh.

1011
01:04:28,064 --> 01:04:29,691
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font>
Story of my life.

1012
01:04:30,166 --> 01:04:33,135
Some bum's always trying to steal
what's mine.

1013
01:04:34,204 --> 01:04:35,671
<font color="#808080">HERBERT:</font>
You gotta dance.

1014
01:04:39,542 --> 01:04:41,203
Come on. Finish him.

1015
01:04:41,878 --> 01:04:43,368
Oh!

1016
01:04:44,381 --> 01:04:46,440
<font color="#D900D9">(INDISTINCT DIALOGUE ON RADIO)</font>

1017
01:04:46,850 --> 01:04:48,681
- Hey, Dad?
- Yeah?

1018
01:04:48,852 --> 01:04:51,343
Mom wants to know when you're gonna
put up the lights.

1019
01:04:51,521 --> 01:04:54,513
As soon as I'm done here.
Can you hand me those wire strippers?

1020
01:04:54,691 --> 01:04:55,851
Yeah.

1021
01:04:56,459 --> 01:04:58,791
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

1022
01:04:58,962 --> 01:05:01,931
Son, your dad's a genius.

1023
01:05:03,433 --> 01:05:04,798
Go tell your mom that.

1024
01:05:06,069 --> 01:05:10,529
So the first one's Pacific Telephone.
The second one's Western Union.

1025
01:05:10,707 --> 01:05:11,935
And that third one...

1026
01:05:12,108 --> 01:05:14,372
- Cohen's.<font color="#808080">
KEELER:</font> That's right.

1027
01:05:14,544 --> 01:05:16,569
That's all there is to it?
Just cut the wire?

1028
01:05:16,746 --> 01:05:20,045
No. You cut the wire, they'd be out
here in an hour to repair it.

1029
01:05:20,216 --> 01:05:22,707
El Dorado Trust is the terminus
of the wire, right?

1030
01:05:22,886 --> 01:05:27,220
So all you gotta do is ping the wire and the
pulse echo will tell you how far away it is.

1031
01:05:27,557 --> 01:05:28,922
Why didn't I think of that?

1032
01:05:29,092 --> 01:05:30,616
Hey, keep an eye out.

1033
01:05:36,633 --> 01:05:38,396
<font color="#D900D9">(CHATTERING)</font>

1034
01:05:41,604 --> 01:05:42,935
What'll it be?

1035
01:05:45,141 --> 01:05:46,472
Remember 75.

1036
01:05:49,779 --> 01:05:52,407
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font>
And bingo.

1037
01:05:52,816 --> 01:05:54,408
You gotta be shitting me.

1038
01:05:54,918 --> 01:05:57,284
<font color="#808080">KEELER:</font> Am I the only one who thinks
this is fucking insane?

1039
01:05:57,454 --> 01:05:59,684
Because there's an alarm,
it goes right to Cohen.

1040
01:05:59,856 --> 01:06:02,188
It'll take me 10 minutes to find it
and disable it.

1041
01:06:02,359 --> 01:06:03,758
You got 5 then.

1042
01:06:03,927 --> 01:06:06,919
Shooting starts, sheriffs are gonna be
all over our asses.

1043
01:06:07,097 --> 01:06:08,462
You sure we can pull this off?

1044
01:06:10,000 --> 01:06:11,024
No.

1045
01:06:11,601 --> 01:06:12,863
Let's do it then.

1046
01:06:17,807 --> 01:06:20,332
<font color="#D900D9">(SINGING "CHICA CHICA BOOM CHIC"
IN PORTUGUESE)</font>

1047
01:06:56,913 --> 01:06:58,380
<font color="#808080">O'MARA:</font> Hey.<font color="#808080">
HARRIS:</font> Hey.

1048
01:06:58,548 --> 01:06:59,913
<font color="#808080">RAMIREZ:</font> Hey.<font color="#808080">
KENNARD:</font> Howdy.

1049
01:07:00,083 --> 01:07:02,074
- Who are you guys?<font color="#808080">
KENNARD:</font> We're the band.

1050
01:07:02,285 --> 01:07:03,547
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font>
Unh!

1051
01:07:04,654 --> 01:07:05,916
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Oh, shit.

1052
01:07:10,427 --> 01:07:12,486
- Keeler?<font color="#808080">
KEELER:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(OVER RADIO)</font> All clear.

1053
01:07:33,116 --> 01:07:34,845
<font color="#D900D9">(CHATTERING)</font>

1054
01:07:36,886 --> 01:07:38,547
<i>Boom, chica, boom-boom-boom-boom-boom</i>

1055
01:07:38,822 --> 01:07:40,255
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font>
Aah!

1056
01:07:43,893 --> 01:07:46,862
All right, everybody, time to go home!
Out!

1057
01:07:47,030 --> 01:07:49,260
Ladies, go on and take
the rest of the night off.

1058
01:07:49,432 --> 01:07:51,627
Come on, ladies. That means you. Get up.

1059
01:07:52,535 --> 01:07:54,127
<font color="#808080">RAMIREZ:</font>
Let's go, ladies. Come on.

1060
01:07:54,337 --> 01:07:56,066
We already took care of that.

1061
01:08:01,911 --> 01:08:03,435
<i>Ch-ch-chica, boom</i>

1062
01:08:16,593 --> 01:08:18,925
<i>Chica, chica, boom, chica boom
Chica, boom-boom-boom</i>

1063
01:08:19,095 --> 01:08:20,722
<i>Boom, chica, boom-boom-boom</i>

1064
01:08:20,897 --> 01:08:21,921
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOT)</font>

1065
01:08:22,098 --> 01:08:23,963
<font color="#808080">SINGER:</font> Aah!<font color="#808080">
O'MARA:</font> Everybody out! Now!

1066
01:08:24,934 --> 01:08:26,060
Everybody out!

1067
01:08:31,441 --> 01:08:32,772
<font color="#D900D9">(PEOPLE SHOUTING)</font>

1068
01:08:53,096 --> 01:08:54,654
My, oh, my.

1069
01:08:55,698 --> 01:08:58,428
What the fuck happened here, Eugene?

1070
01:08:58,601 --> 01:09:01,502
We don't know, Mr. Cohen.
Right now, I'm coordinating the...

1071
01:09:01,671 --> 01:09:04,435
"Coordinating"? What's this coordinating?

1072
01:09:04,607 --> 01:09:05,938
Take the dog.

1073
01:09:06,109 --> 01:09:07,098
No, the deputy.

1074
01:09:11,948 --> 01:09:14,007
This how you take care of business?

1075
01:09:14,184 --> 01:09:15,947
You motherfucker!

1076
01:09:16,119 --> 01:09:20,522
You will find the cocksuckers
that did this to me!

1077
01:09:20,690 --> 01:09:22,715
You will find them!

1078
01:09:24,160 --> 01:09:25,684
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Drink. Come on.

1079
01:09:25,862 --> 01:09:27,887
- Look, look. Come on.<font color="#808080">
RAMIREZ:</font> Shut up.

1080
01:09:28,064 --> 01:09:30,532
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font>
Come on, you son of a... Drink.

1081
01:09:30,700 --> 01:09:31,940
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
No, it's right here, man.

1082
01:09:32,068 --> 01:09:34,036
Drink it. Don't be scared, don't be scared.

1083
01:09:34,204 --> 01:09:38,504
Our young Señor Ramirez is drunker
than a peach orchard sow.

1084
01:09:38,675 --> 01:09:40,040
- Let me tap you.
- No, I'm good.

1085
01:09:40,210 --> 01:09:41,199
You sure?

1086
01:09:41,377 --> 01:09:42,708
It's not good right now.

1087
01:09:43,379 --> 01:09:44,869
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Sarge, come here for a second.

1088
01:09:45,048 --> 01:09:47,881
- Come on, everybody. Get over here.
- Come on, sarge.

1089
01:09:48,051 --> 01:09:49,382
Sarge, come here.

1090
01:09:49,552 --> 01:09:50,644
To the sarge.

1091
01:09:50,820 --> 01:09:52,981
For bringing us all home safe.

1092
01:09:53,156 --> 01:09:57,525
You're a bull in a china shop, but we'd
follow you anywhere. To the sarge.

1093
01:09:57,694 --> 01:10:01,027
No, look, this victory belongs to all of us.

1094
01:10:01,464 --> 01:10:06,197
You know, I've run with a lot of outfits,
but none better than you group of misfits.

1095
01:10:06,402 --> 01:10:07,391
<font color="#D900D9">(ALL LAUGHING)</font>

1096
01:10:07,570 --> 01:10:08,559
Cheers.

1097
01:10:08,738 --> 01:10:11,400
<font color="#808080">HARRIS:</font> To the Gangster Squad.<font color="#808080">
RAMIREZ:</font> The Gangster Squad.

1098
01:10:20,516 --> 01:10:22,347
How much did they get away with?

1099
01:10:22,986 --> 01:10:24,078
Nothing.

1100
01:10:24,587 --> 01:10:26,612
Neddy says they didn't take the money.

1101
01:10:33,396 --> 01:10:34,988
They're cops.

1102
01:10:38,101 --> 01:10:41,093
Chief Parker put them up to it.

1103
01:10:42,538 --> 01:10:47,407
I've had it with that sadistic,
Bible-thumping boozer.

1104
01:10:49,112 --> 01:10:50,545
He's done.

1105
01:10:51,514 --> 01:10:54,039
We never had that kind of trouble before.

1106
01:10:54,884 --> 01:10:56,579
Trust me, Karl.

1107
01:10:57,220 --> 01:11:01,054
I've bought myself enough cops.
I know what I'm talking about.

1108
01:11:02,659 --> 01:11:05,822
These guys are a special brand.

1109
01:11:06,329 --> 01:11:08,627
They're hard cases, not interested in money.

1110
01:11:08,798 --> 01:11:11,232
A cop that's not for sale
is like a dog with rabies.

1111
01:11:11,401 --> 01:11:13,665
There's no medicine for it, you just gotta...

1112
01:11:15,104 --> 01:11:16,571
...put him down.

1113
01:11:19,175 --> 01:11:20,608
Heh.

1114
01:11:23,846 --> 01:11:25,814
Somebody peached to them.

1115
01:11:28,117 --> 01:11:30,483
Somebody up and turned rat on me!

1116
01:11:32,155 --> 01:11:35,420
There's ears in this fucking house!
Find them!

1117
01:11:36,693 --> 01:11:38,752
The slut cluck bitches!

1118
01:11:39,429 --> 01:11:43,627
Come on. We need to get you out of here
before he runs out of pretty things to break.

1119
01:11:44,100 --> 01:11:47,194
Now, you don't ever need to come
back here, Miss Grace. Not ever.

1120
01:11:49,939 --> 01:11:52,134
<font color="#D900D9">(DEVICE BLEEPING)</font>

1121
01:12:04,220 --> 01:12:07,300
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font> <font color="#D900D9">(OVER RADIO)</font> <i>Wrevock's gonna
pick up the shipment tonight in Chinatown.</i>

1122
01:12:07,457 --> 01:12:09,084
<i>Use the laundry truck.</i>

1123
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:10,690
No, wait, you gotta hear this.

1124
01:12:13,229 --> 01:12:17,029
<font color="#808080">COHEN:</font> <i>You don't make this deal,
we're finished, you hear me? Done.</i>

1125
01:12:17,200 --> 01:12:19,498
<i>That hit on Slapsy's is still killing us.</i>

1126
01:12:19,669 --> 01:12:22,570
<i>Wrevock's gonna pick up the shipment
tonight in Chinatown.</i>

1127
01:12:22,739 --> 01:12:26,038
<i>Use the laundry truck. Don't fuck it up.
I need this.</i>

1128
01:12:26,409 --> 01:12:27,398
We hurt him.

1129
01:12:28,311 --> 01:12:31,803
He is bleeding cash. Desperate enough
to do this out in the open.

1130
01:12:31,981 --> 01:12:34,814
We intercept that dope,
he is dead in the water.

1131
01:12:36,185 --> 01:12:39,814
You know, I signed up for this...

1132
01:12:40,656 --> 01:12:41,680
...ahem...

1133
01:12:41,858 --> 01:12:46,386
...so that I could tell my boy that I
at least tried to do something about it.

1134
01:12:46,562 --> 01:12:49,656
But I hope he never finds out about
all the things we've done.

1135
01:12:49,832 --> 01:12:51,527
Con, we did what we had to do.

1136
01:12:51,701 --> 01:12:55,637
Can you remind me of the difference
between us and them?

1137
01:12:57,673 --> 01:13:00,005
Because at this point, I can't tell anymore.

1138
01:13:00,543 --> 01:13:03,239
You want to find a witness to sign
their own death warrant?

1139
01:13:03,413 --> 01:13:08,441
Con, look, this is the only way
we can beat him. The only way.

1140
01:13:11,521 --> 01:13:12,715
Okay.

1141
01:13:17,093 --> 01:13:20,688
All right, look,
I need you on the wire tonight.

1142
01:13:20,863 --> 01:13:22,023
- Okay?
- Oh, no.

1143
01:13:22,198 --> 01:13:26,100
In case Cohen has a change of plan.
It's all right, Con.

1144
01:13:26,269 --> 01:13:28,897
You sit this one out. We can handle it.

1145
01:13:29,672 --> 01:13:30,764
All right?

1146
01:13:32,275 --> 01:13:33,367
Okay.

1147
01:13:45,922 --> 01:13:46,946
<font color="#808080">JERRY:</font>
Hey.

1148
01:13:48,224 --> 01:13:49,555
You wanted to talk to me?

1149
01:13:50,326 --> 01:13:51,793
He thinks somebody ratted.

1150
01:13:52,195 --> 01:13:53,219
